            <ArticleTitle>Understanding and treating childhood bellyaches.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>97-104</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Symptom-based diagnoses for most childhood bellyaches may be applied at the first visit, reducing family anxiety and healthcare spending. Primary care clinicians are able to diagnose and treat these disorders effectively. The promise of continuing availability is essential and assures that no disease will be missed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
